ents distinguish raising money, pooling risk, purchasing services, and paying providers.", "children": [{"id": "48a59658-14b9-46bb-928b-cb57d45147a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Taxes, premiums, and out-of-pocket payment"}, {"id": "26205f2a-006a-41b9-90f7-f35901ccf681", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk pooling"}, {"id": "a878904c-8246-44f9-9be6-815b3b853b43", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefit design"}, {"id": "8e943c48-dbd1-4149-8118-72520928834f", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic purchasing"}]}, {"id": "d897ace6-517e-4f61-9292-416b608c6fa4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Provider payment and incentives", "description": "Payment rules shape volume, coordination, selection, quality, and financial risk.", "children": [{"id": "817727f9-b6f6-44e5-ab29-623ac0394ec0", "type": "concept", "title": "Fee-for-service"}, {"id": "df70e0c1-4dbf-4101-b068-ebec2e8603d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Capitation and global budgets"}, {"id": "f0722d8a-d199-4946-a283-e646e7ae1db6", "type": "concept", "title": "Bundled payment"}, {"id": "87b4533f-95af-434e-bc99-7b644b4d9ce8", "type": "concept", "title": "Value-based purchasing and pay-for-performance"}]}, {"id": "d12a633a-ba63-40c9-950f-13e9391925f5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost and expenditure analysis", "description": "Students connect prices, utilization, intensity, administration, and population need to spending.", "children": [{"id": "1c46e0c9-fc21-4705-889a-87b603fa445a", "type": "concept", "title": "National health expenditures"}, {"id": "4539f444-0b02-4a6e-ad84-0472edde174a", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit price versus volume"}, {"id": "9c1af70b-da81-4561-a298-e5fc7f8c582a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost shifting and market power"}, {"id": "ad8b8182-0520-4205-8347-96042deb1ad0", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget impact and fiscal sustainability"}]}]}, {"id": "e58af264-4bba-4523-b5e3-7a5bc1efe858", "type": "topic", "title": "Coverage, Access, and Universal Health Protection", "description": "Examines insurance, eligibility, affordability, provider availability, nonfinancial barriers, and policy strategies for equitable access and financial protection.", "children": [{"id": "fcd751db-cd3c-487b-98c2-c116e5ad3e6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coverage architecture", "description": "Students compare public programs, employer coverage, individual markets, and safety-net arrangements.", "children": [{"id": "059ab567-e8f0-4ce3-b25f-016ec5a1a2bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicare and Medicaid"}, {"id": "f758d569-840c-4da7-bca6-0c8e567275a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Employer-sponsored insurance"}, {"id": "76dbf3ac-2119-4e3d-be4b-dfe753b48377", "type": "concept", "title": "Marketplace coverage"}, {"id": "4e70a648-fc7f-415a-b96d-f8377b4a0cd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Uninsured and underinsured populations"}]}, {"id": "be44e51e-31b6-4a3f-86e2-b5a8e44e4bec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Access dimensions", "description": "Insurance does not guarantee timely, acceptable, geographically available care.", "children": [{"id": "8df21cbd-4f88-46ba-b91b-9d8100dfca7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Affordability"}, {"id": "ee196471-ff09-4364-a119-70e9fa462cd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability and workforce"}, {"id": "664a8354-6774-48e6-bb74-a80b66c9c3f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Geographic accessibility"}, {"id": "578de477-eff8-45df-910e-06e8f208264d", "type": "concept", "title": "Acceptability, language, and trust"}]}, {"id": "9f11e1b8-6a1d-4196-8106-630cfdd0cd21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial protection and equity", "description": "Coverage policy redistributes resources and exposure to medical financial risk.", "children": [{"id": "d18c2de5-370a-41b1-9589-54e0fe1d429a", "type": "concept", "title": "Premiums and cost sharing"}, {"id": "b2f1ba5a-6737-474b-87c1-a3f8f1b8aff0", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical debt"}, {"id": "681d06c9-699d-484e-a078-a5239da37639", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefit adequacy"}, {"id": "860eef5e-8c97-4b0e-8080-a871d2fba5b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal coverage strategies"}]}]}, {"id": "37a19cf9-cbe3-428c-b878-c5a02a631d96", "type": "topic", "title": "Quality, Patient Safety, and Performance Policy", "description": "Develops the ability to define, measure, compare, and improve quality and safety without confusing easily measured activity with meaningful outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "02a388f6-5e2e-4836-9066-ca4f48fda218", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality frameworks", "description": "Students define quality before selecting measures or interventions.", "children": [{"id": "c5cc9940-71a1-45ed-aef3-3b1e39baa5e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Structure, process, and outcome"}, {"id": "bcf8d688-d15f-40d0-871a-a0790313622f", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, effectiveness, timeliness, efficiency, equity, and patient-centeredness"}, {"id": "03ab871d-c709-41ac-9630-5ff59602f6b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Population versus clinical quality"}, {"id": "549c4177-6078-45fb-8292-50193f19b569", "type": "concept", "title": "Experience and reported outcomes"}]}, {"id": "4a454586-d0c0-48ce-ba89-0f2bb1f67540", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement and accountability", "description": "Measures can improve transparency while also creating gaming and burden.", "children": [{"id": "f185b908-38fa-4629-b997-029b2adc1f05", "type": "concept", "title": "Numerators, denominators, and risk adjustment"}, {"id": "907f6d56-d9ae-4e34-9663-30e28845aee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboards and public reporting"}, {"id": "be658c22-5b05-4b12-af9b-3c056c1f6f6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Accreditation and regulation"}, {"id": "2dad26ed-c570-4af5-9281-e285f81df11a", "type": "concept", "title": "Unintended consequences"}]}, {"id": "09ff6e7b-40d7-4633-93cb-f5079a6e9977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Improvement methods", "description": "Students use systems thinking to test changes rather than blame individuals.", "children": [{"id": "02060916-ea04-4381-a541-6a195d8a7f61", "type": "concept", "title": "Process mapping"}, {"id": "4d3b2ef6-569e-410a-8ec6-c063bdb714e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Root-cause analysis"}, {"id": "ce5ea119-6608-4f86-afe4-f613f6cde96d", "type": "concept", "title": "Plan–Do–Study–Act"}, {"id": "1a49edd9-7eef-4c18-9eb6-51093078d833", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing measures and learning systems"}]}]}, {"id": "4f603f65-e60b-42d2-b7d7-75c10effbcd4", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Health Law, Ethics, and Human Rights", "description": "Provides a framework for authority, rights, due process, proportionality, privacy, emergency powers, and ethical allocation in population health.", "children": [{"id": "6f22b3f2-f700-4050-83ac-f6788a6e7613", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Legal foundations", "description": "Students identify authority and limits before recommending government action.", "children": [{"id": "cdb32b33-2798-4a47-84ad-8646780f9eb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Police powers"}, {"id": "bfbb6b85-aed2-4afe-963c-ba876e8dc58e", "type": "concept", "title": "Commerce and spending powers"}, {"id": "3f7b7b2f-9051-4365-86b3-ef82a3e8e66a", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative law"}, {"id": "1e13cb30-f967-4eac-a5f6-e67d65496cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial review"}]}, {"id": "23dbe4c6-64e8-4f85-8f30-aa1027653fbc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights and due process", "description": "Population benefit must be balanced with liberty, privacy, equality, and fair procedure.", "children": [{"id": "79951300-0877-48d2-ba09-a6ea267fe50f", "type": "concept", "title": "Substantive and procedural due process"}, {"id": "fe5c31d9-d59e-4f83-b6d2-a59b6050b1a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Equal protection"}, {"id": "acebeb2c-ce15-409f-9aa8-fdc5deca0916", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy and confidentiality"}, {"id": "c89493c6-7c97-4357-948c-ea5b89ba2631", "type": "concept", "title": "Least-restrictive means"}]}, {"id": "41bf0400-3704-4888-b11a-6f9f54f3358f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical analysis", "description": "Ethics makes values and burdens visible when law alone does not resolve a choice.", "children": [{"id": "5991d27b-1054-4d88-8b3a-85e43ad14ad0", "type": "concept", "title": "Utility and harm prevention"}, {"id": "60a955b5-ec92-4538-a69b-b8173b3b4675", "type": "concept", "title": "Justice and equity"}, {"id": "d6fea102-6e6b-428a-93c6-c907e5b1882a", "type": "concept", "title": "Autonomy and solidarity"}, {"id": "238b6a2d-71cc-4139-b2a7-120334c20693", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportionality, reciprocity, and transparency"}]}]}, {"id": "665692d3-a78c-4339-9d82-1d1d1de34114", "type": "topic", "title": "Politics, Power, Stakeholders, and Advocacy", "description": "Makes visible how institutions, interests, ideology, evidence, narrative, media, lobbying, and public participation shape health decisions.", "children": [{"id": "460268aa-b1c7-4110-812b-eac4ba8ff9b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and power", "description": "Students examine formal authority and informal influence over agendas, evidence, and resources.", "children": [{"id": "c0fdefb9-4d37-4409-8803-ee2d7e1668dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Veto points"}, {"id": "3534c9bb-4033-4211-bc78-aa419c3c0164", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest groups and lobbying"}, {"id": "17d6310e-c023-43d9-b1e6-341d1abe22c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional and industry power"}, {"id": "30edbed5-d51c-4794-9ef1-cd37c190c0d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bureaucratic and expert authority"}]}, {"id": "b83b2159-aad7-433a-b895-01dd36f39cc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public opinion and communication", "description": "Narratives, trust, identity, media, and polling influence policy feasibility.", "children": [{"id": "6c3d9a92-7a68-4232-92ac-156737c84d23", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing and message testing"}, {"id": "c8081c2e-4651-4e21-b100-23e942906332", "type": "concept", "title": "Misinformation"}, {"id": "49cc2ea3-95d1-4df9-bc74-41d1fd96524e", "type": "concept", "ti